SuZero AI is a 5D chess AlphaZero project. Substantial portions of its search
core are derived from KataGo (https://github.com/lightvector/KataGo),
Copyright (c) 2025 David J Wu ("lightvector") and/or other authors of that
repository, which is distributed under the MIT License. The Python trainer
reimplements training-schedule methods from KataGo's python/train.py. KataGo's
upstream copyright notice and license text are reproduced in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and must be retained in redistributions.

Third-party components used by this repository. Each component remains under
its own license; the list below is a summary, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
contains the full upstream notices:

- KataGo (MIT) - search core and training methods.
  https://github.com/lightvector/KataGo
- 5dchess_engine (BSD 2-Clause, Copyright (c) 2024-2026, ftxi) - rules engine
  and native replay UI, vendored under 5dchess_engine-main/.
  https://github.com/ftxi/5dchess_engine
- ONNX Runtime (MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation) - linked at build
  time from a user-provided SDK; not vendored in this repository.
  https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
- very_small ONNX model and legacy LSTM checkpoint compatibility (BSD
  2-Clause, Copyright (c) 2024-2026, ftxi) - derived from 5dc_ml.
  https://github.com/ftxi/5dc_ml
